  "details": "- CVE-2026-106587: sshd did not clear AuthorizedPrincipalsFile,\n  TrustedUserCAKeys and Banner when a Match block set them to \"none\", so\n  the global value stayed in effect before authentication; clear them in\n  the pre-auth part of copy_set_server_options(). Backport upstream\n  commit 526fd277.\n- CVE-2026-106586: sshd dropped the authorized_keys \"restrict\" flag when\n  merging key and certificate options, which could re-enable features such\n  as tunnel forwarding; OR the restricted flag in sshauthopt_merge().\n  Backport upstream commit 991f1f31.\n- CVE-2026-106552: sftp(1) accepted an empty file name from a server\n  directory listing and could pick \"..\" or the local root as an implicit\n  download destination; reject empty names and map \"..\" and remote roots\n  to \".\". Backport upstream commit c07ea218.\n- CVE-2026-106584: ssh-keygen(1) converted certificate validity dates\n  without letting mktime() decide DST, giving expiry times off by an hour;\n  set tm_isdst to -1 in parse_absolute_time(). Backport upstream commit\n  aef20dfe.\n- CVE-2026-106582: compressed SSH sessions used the zlib LZ77 dictionary\n  coder, exposing a compression side channel; use Huffman-only\n  compression for outgoing packets. Backport upstream commit 1d5340fc.",
